# KNOWN GAP — CRITICAL. A CONTAINER LITERAL mints its ELEMENT TYPE from the
# SOURCE OPERAND before that operand is materialized, so a borrow-typed source
# produces `Vector[Ptr(T)]`: 8-byte slots with no elem drop/clone/materialize
# vtable. The correctly-cloned value is then stored 8-bytes-wide and freed.
#
# NO for-loop, NO `&` sigil, NO patch required — this is HEAD, ordinary syntax.
#
# Measured 2026-08-18:
#     gg check                 -> OK: no semantic errors   (rc 0)
#     gg build / --backend=llvm-> rc 0, both lanes
#     run                      -> rc 0; len() reports 1 and the element reads
#                                 back EMPTY. Under ASan: abort,
#                                 allocation-size-too-big 0xbebebebebebebec0
#                                 (0xbe = freed poison read as a length)
#     ggdef                    -> prints `bb`, the CORRECT answer
#
# Core #8: one accepted program, three lanes, the ORACLE is right and BOTH
# production backends are wrong.
#
# Sites: `src/ir/lowering/exprs/collections.rs` — the array, set and dict
# literal arms each call `infer_operand_type_full` on the pre-materialization
# operand. Core #15e Q5 (emission ORDER — *when* the destination type is minted
# relative to materialization) with Layering rule 4 inverted.
#
# ⚠ WHY THE EXISTING GUARD DOES NOT CATCH IT: `Ptr(T)` is not
# `is_resource_type`, so the bogus element type LAUNDERS the value straight past
# the fatal `ShallowCopyOfResource` validator — the guard that exists for
# exactly this class cannot see it.
#
# ⚠ THE OWNERSHIP MACHINERY IS NOT AT FAULT. `ensure_owned_at_consuming_arg`
# fires correctly and the clone IS emitted (verified in the generated C). It is
# the SLOT that is wrong, not the value.
#
# ⚠ NOT a for-loop defect. Track E spent five review generations mis-locating
# this as its own "safe floor" step; that step composes ASan-clean once THIS
# lands, so this is Track E's PRECONDITION.
#
# INTENDED: prints `1` then `bb` on both backends, matching ggdef.
#
# Wired test: known_gap_container_literal_borrow_elem_type (tests/integration.rs,
# #[ignore]d). A measured prototype exists — one accessor (`owned_slot_type`,
# resolving `Ptr(T)`->`T` when `clone_fn_for_ptr(inner).is_some()`) plus the
# three literal call sites; 9 red cells went green and matched ggdef on both
# backends. ⚠ The full C sweep was never completed against it and MUST be run
# before it lands.
Vector[String] mk():
    Vector[String] v = ["aa", "bb"]
    auto s = v.get(1).unwrap()
    Vector[String] out = [s]
    return out

void main():
    Vector[String] r = mk()
    print(r.len())
    print(r.get(0).unwrap())
